# Identifying the Base Number

When we know the result of a power (like a square or a cube), we can work backward to find the base number[cite: 7]. Use your knowledge of perfect squares and cubes to find the value of $x$ in each problem below[cite: 7].

> **Remember:**
> - If $x^2 = n$, then $x = \sqrt{n}$[cite: 7].
> - If $x^3 = n$, then $x = \sqrt[3]{n}$[cite: 7].

